@startuml Message_Broker_Architecture

title Message Broker — Async Flow + Pub/Sub Pattern

skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontSize 13

actor User
participant "Front-End\nService" as FE
queue "Message Broker\n(Orders Channel)" as MB
participant "Fulfillment\nService" as Fulfill
participant "Analytics\nService" as Analytics
participant "Push Notification\nService" as Push
participant "Review/Survey\nService" as Review

User -> FE : Place order
FE -> MB : Publish "OrderPlaced" event
FE --> User : Immediate acknowledgment\n(no waiting)

MB -> Fulfill : Deliver message (subscribed)
Fulfill -> Fulfill : Reserve ticket, charge card
Fulfill --> User : Async confirmation email\n(sent later)

MB -> Analytics : Deliver message (subscribed)
Analytics -> Analytics : Analyze purchase pattern

MB -> Push : Deliver message (subscribed)
Push --> User : Push notification

MB -> Review : Deliver message (subscribed)
Review -> Review : Schedule review request

note over MB
  All 3 extra services (Analytics,
  Push, Review) added later via
  Pub/Sub - ZERO changes needed
  to existing Front-End/Fulfillment code
end note

note over FE, Fulfill
  Traffic spike handling:
  Front-End just decrements stock
  counter; MB queues real orders
  to be processed one by one
end note

@enduml
